<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Traben-Trarbach</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Trarbach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Traben-Trarbach is a wine town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, formed in 1904 by uniting Traben and Trarbach on opposite banks. Trarbach was the centre of the Rear County of Sponheim, overlooked by the Grevenburg castle, and later a leading Moselle wine-trading town, known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/art-nouveau">Art Nouveau</a> buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/traben-trarbach.jpg" alt="Traben-Trarbach" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carsten Steger · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_image_of_the_Moselle_in_Traben-Trarbach_(view_from_the_south).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
